What it is: A highly specialized compilation flag used inside wasm-bindgen.

How it works: WebAssembly engines traditionally could only hold numbers.
"Reference Types" is a modern WASM feature that allows a WebAssembly module to hold onto
a native JavaScript object pointer (externref) directly inside its execution stack.
This flag tells the compiler: "The browser we are targeting is modern enough to
handle raw JS object references natively without manual array indexing!"

